# Local disposable stack data (Docker Compose — see
# docs/architecture/docker-compose-stack.md "Persistence, lifecycle, and
# reset"). Database and object-storage data live ONLY in Docker named
# volumes (<project>_postgres-data / <project>_storage-data), never in
# this working tree, so there is nothing here to ignore for those: no
# service bind-mounts a writable data directory from the repository.
#
# The rules below cover the generated application-artifact directories
# the required structure reserves at the repository root
# (context/project-structure.md's storage/ entry: uploads, exports,
# temp). Those directories do not exist yet and no application adapter
# writes to them — these rules are deliberately narrow and defensive, so
# runtime output can never become a tracked artifact if one is added
# later. Each keeps a committed .gitkeep possible, so the rule can never
# hide an intentionally-tracked placeholder.
/storage/uploads/**
!/storage/uploads/.gitkeep
/storage/exports/**
!/storage/exports/.gitkeep
/storage/temp/**
!/storage/temp/.gitkeep
